# Commits use commit.bat

When the user asks to commit, or to commit and push, run `python/commit.bat`. Do not call `git add` / `git commit` / `git push` yourself. The script bumps `python/version.json` before it commits.

- Commit only: `commit.bat "description"`
- Commit and push: `commit.bat -p "description"`

Run it from `python/` (the script switches to its own folder and expects `app.py` there). Pass one description string. The script then asks `Final commit message [Enter keeps draft]:`. Send a blank line so that draft is accepted as-is.

```powershell
cmd /c "echo.| commit.bat -p `"Short description of why this changed`""
```

Working directory: the repo's `python` folder.

Still check status and diff before choosing the description. Do not commit secrets. Do not force-push. Do not skip hooks.
